              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Express both bottles using equal total volumes before adding the water and cordial amounts.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Choose an equal volume of $70$ mL for each bottle, since $70$ is a common multiple of $7$ and $10$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Bottle 1 water}&=\\frac{2}{7}\\times70=20\\text{ mL}\\\\\\text{Bottle 1 cordial}&=\\frac{5}{7}\\times70=50\\text{ mL}\\\\\\text{Bottle 2 water}&=\\frac{3}{10}\\times70=21\\text{ mL}\\\\\\text{Bottle 2 cordial}&=\\frac{7}{10}\\times70=49\\text{ mL}\\\\\\text{Combined water : cordial}&=(20+21):(50+49)\\\\\\text{Combined water : cordial}&=41:99\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
